# Code Quality

Always:

- use TypeScript strict mode
- use named exports and absolute imports (`@/…`)
- validate every input with a zod DTO through the global ZodValidationPipe
- return response DTOs, never ORM entities
- throw `AppException` with an `ErrorCode`
- read config through the typed config, never `process.env`
- inject dependencies through the constructor
- sort object keys and interface members alphabetically
- write self-explanatory code; comment only non-obvious decisions (why, not what)

Avoid:

- any, `as` casts of external data, non-null `!` on external data
- class-validator / class-transformer (zod is the validator)
- raw SQL string concatenation
- `console.log` (use the injected logger)
- business logic in controllers
- `new` for injectable services
- static mutable state
- unbounded queries on list endpoints
- redundant comments, section banners, commented-out code
